course: dictionary
lesson: 2419
title: A cyclist is a person who rides a bicycle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a word by looking at its parts. Cyclist comes from cycle, a short word for bicycle, and the ending -ist means a person who does something. So a cyclist is a person who rides a bicycle. Check it in a sentence: «Cyclists ride in the same direction as the traffic.» Swap in the meaning: people who ride bicycles ride in the same direction as the traffic. That still makes sense.
explain: The sentences also show where cyclists are. «A cyclist could not stop in time» tells you a cyclist can be on a road with cars, vans and lorries. Clues like this help you picture the word before you even check the meaning. Notice that cyclist means the rider, the person, not the bicycle itself.
explain: Words can also tell you what a cyclist does on a journey. Maths problems may ask how far, how fast or how long a cyclist rides, and cyclists can race in sport on roads and tracks. When you see the word, ask yourself: who is doing the riding, and what is the riding for?
fact: A cyclist is a person who rides a bicycle.
fact: Cyclists is the plural, and it means more than one cyclist.
fact: Safe cyclists wear helmets, use lights at night, signal with their arms and use cycle lanes.
fact: «A big truck or lorry has blind spots where the driver cannot see a bike at all.»
fact: Cyclists can race in sport on roads and on tracks.
exercise: What is a cyclist? | A vehicle with two wheels and a motor | *A person who rides a bicycle | A person who drives a lorry | A wheel on a bicycle
exercise: «Cyclists ride in the same direction as the traffic.» What does traffic mean here? | Sweets sold at the shop | A quiet path in the park | *The vehicles moving along the road | The people who ride bicycles only
exercise: Why must a cyclist never ride up the inside of a truck at a junction? | Because trucks are faster than bicycles | Because trucks only drive at night | *Because the driver cannot see a bike in its blind spots | Because cyclists are not allowed on roads
test: Which word means more than one cyclist? | cycle | cyclistss | *cyclists | cyclistic
test: «Cyclists sometimes race in sport.» Where do cyclists race? | *On roads and tracks | Inside a house | In the sea | On the moon
exam: Which safety step should a cyclist take at night? | *Use lights | Ride without hands | Ride on the pavement at full speed | Wear a blindfold
